  "full_text": "So at Ticketmaster there were pretty much the boss woman there was Laura Hunter and she was pretty flat chested and I spent some time in close proximity to her and I don't know if it rewired me or what but after World War I there was the era of the flappers and Diana Coward, right? I don't know. So sometimes I think some of this is... I don't know, that's crazy, but the epic rap battles seem like they're all about me, and I don't know if I came through the CIA channels or what, but I remember my dad bought a quarter, invested some money in a quarter horse called Wonder J. Woman back in, oh, I'd say about 1980, something, one, two, we were up in Washington State, It was just kind of, someone at work had a racehorse and it was named Wonder J. Woman and my dad put some money into it. I think it didn't go anywhere. And anyway, so it's kind of interesting.",
